POINTER: The mesher samples light from up to 4 neighbors (the face's 4 corners + the center neighbor) to compute per-vertex skylight/blocklight — this is how light gradients appear across a face, and it's the mechanism to extend if adding new light sources (lab/lite/src/demos/minecraft/mesher.ts, the `skySum`/`blkSum` accumulation block)
POINTER: The three-batch split (opaque/cutout/blend) means any new render mode (e.g. emissive, depth-only) would need a fourth batch and a corresponding pipeline in the chunk renderer (lab/lite/src/demos/minecraft/mesher.ts, `batchFor(cd.renderMode)`)
