// Voxel surface material: samples the block atlas, then lights it from baked
// per-vertex terms carried in `color` (r = ambient occlusion, g = skylight
// visibility, b = blocklight) combined in the shader with the dynamic day-night
// sun/ambient and a warm torch tint, and applies linear distance fog toward the
// sky horizon colour. Three variants share one shader via defines:
//   - "opaque": solid blocks (depth write, back-face cull).
//   - "cutout": leaves/cactus — alpha-tested discard, still depth-writing.
//   - "blend":  water/glass/ice — alpha blended, no depth write, gentle wave shimmer.
//
// Vertex positions are world-space (chunk meshes sit at the origin) so fog and the
// water shimmer can use the world coordinate directly.
```

POINTER: The vertex shader packs four baked terms into the `color` attribute (r=AO, g=skylight, b=blocklight, a=fluid/sway flag) — this is the data contract between mesher.ts and the shader, important if extending block types or adding new per-vertex terms (voxel-material.ts, vertexSource())
POINTER: Water Fresnel reflection uses a `cameraPos` uniform updated per-frame via `setVoxelCameraPos` — relevant if adding reflective materials or extending the water sim (voxel-material.ts, setVoxelCameraPos)
POINTER: The three material variants share one WGSL shader source discriminated by a `mode` parameter with inline conditional code for wave shimmer (blend) and wind sway (cutout) — this pattern matters if adding a fourth render mode or modifying per-mode vertex behavior (voxel-material.ts, vertexSource())

